<title>BELGIUM: Fischler to report Monday on veterinary talks.</title>
<headline>Fischler to report Monday on veterinary talks.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler will report to farm ministers on Monday on progress towards concluding veterinary equivalency agreements with various trade partners, a Dutch EU presidency official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Fischler will make a verbal report on the state of negotiations,&quot; the official said ahead of the one-day Farm Council.</p>
<p>The Commission has set an April 1, 1997, deadline for reaching agreement with the United States, Canada, Australia and various Latin American and other countries.</p>
<p>The first agreement -- with New Zealand -- on the mutual recognition of veterinary and plant health standards and inspection rules, was signed in December.</p>
<p>The Commission is planning to present to member states early in 1997 a proposal for an agreement with the Czech Republic.</p>
</text>
